menu "Xiaozhi Assistant"

config USE_EMOTE_MESSAGE_STYLE
    bool "Use rawdraw 1bpp rendering (no LVGL)"
    default y
    help
        When enabled, the display uses rawdraw 1bpp framebuffer rendering
        instead of LVGL. This is the recommended mode for the ZecTrix
        S3 E-Paper 4.2 board as LVGL causes frequent crashes.

config BOARD_TYPE_ZECTRIX_S3_EPAPER_4_2
    bool "zectrix-s3-epaper-4.2 FT firmware"
    default y
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    help
        This local repository has been reduced to a single FT-only firmware
        for the zectrix-s3-epaper-4.2 board.

choice ZECTRIX_EPD_PANEL_TYPE
    prompt "ZecTrix EPD panel type"
    default ZECTRIX_EPD_PANEL_4COLOR_SSD2683
    depends on BOARD_TYPE_ZECTRIX_S3_EPAPER_4_2
    help
        Select the e-paper panel connected to the board. The 4-color option
        keeps the existing 1bpp UI framebuffer and converts it to the SSD2683
        2bpp wire format during refresh.

config ZECTRIX_EPD_PANEL_1BPP
    bool "1bpp black/white EPD"

config ZECTRIX_EPD_PANEL_4COLOR_SSD2683
    bool "4-color BWRY SSD2683 EPD"

endchoice

config AUTONOMY_ENABLED
    bool "Semi-autonomous rendering (autonomy profile + Open-Meteo)"
    default n
    help
        Off by default, and that default is the rollout gate rather than a
        preference.

        When off, this build advertises no "autonomy.profile.v1" capability,
        brings up no profile store, answers the profile and local-render routes
        with 404 autonomy_unsupported, and never composes a frame for itself. A
        tower reads the capability list and reports the gap structurally instead
        of offering controls that would do nothing. The device is exactly the
        push target it was before the feature existed.

        When on, the device may compose its own panel from a profile the tower
        pushed, and may make at most one HTTPS request per wake to Open-Meteo
        for a forecast. Even then nothing happens until autonomy.enabled is set
        through the config API: this flag decides whether the feature can be
        turned on at all, and that field decides whether it is.

        Note what this flag does NOT do: the autonomy translation units are
        still compiled and linked. It gates the feature's reachability, not its
        presence in the binary. DASHBOARD_MINIMAL_UI is the other kind of
        switch and the difference is deliberate.

config ZECTRIX_EPD_4COLOR_BOOT_TEST_PATTERN
    bool "Show 4-color EPD test pattern at boot"
    default n
    depends on ZECTRIX_EPD_PANEL_4COLOR_SSD2683
    help
        Show black/white/red/yellow vertical bars once during display
        initialization so a newly connected 4-color panel can be verified.

endmenu
